{"tool_name":"igvtools","contents":["biocontainers","bioschemas","biotools","bioconda","oeb"],"fetched_metadata":{"bioconda":{"name":"igvtools","version":"2.17.3","home":"http://www.broadinstitute.org/igv/","license":"MIT","summary":"Command line tools for IGV","identifiers":["biotools:IGVtools"],"build":{"noarch":"generic","number":0,"run_exports":[null]},"requirements":{"run":["openjdk >=17"]},"source_url":"http://data.broadinstitute.org/igv/projects/downloads/2.17/IGV_2.17.3.zip","test":{"commands":["igvtools help"]}},"biocontainers":{"name":"igvtools","identifiers":["biotools:IGVtools","doi:10.1093/bib/bbs017"],"license":"MIT","summary":"Command line tools for igv","home_url":"http://www.broadinstitute.org/igv/","keywords":["Computational Biology","Computer Graphics","Data Display","Data Mining","Databases, Genetic","Genomics","High-Throughput Nucleotide Sequencing","Humans","Information Storage and Retrieval","Sequence Alignment","User-Computer Interface","Sequence analysis"],"manually_check":true,"total_pulls":5482},"biotools":{"id":"igvtools","home":"https://software.broadinstitute.org/software/igv/igvtools","license":"MIT","summary":"The igvtools utility provides a set of tools for pre-processing data files.","addition_date":"2017-08-20T15:57:32Z","last_update_date":"2019-09-04T08:38:11Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool","Plug-in"],"collections":["Animal and Crop Genomics"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:igvtools","credit":[{"typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"],"url":"http://software.broadinstitute.org/software/igv/?q=contact"}],"documentation":[{"type":["General"],"url":"https://software.broadinstitute.org/software/igv/igvtools_commandline"}],"edit_permission":{"authors":["animalandcropgenomics"],"type":"group"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Formatting","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0335"},{"term":"Sequence feature comparison","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0256"}]}],"name":"IGVtools","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"admin","publication":[{"doi":"10.1093/bib/bbs017","metadata":{"abstract":"Data visualization is an essential component of genomic data analysis. However, the size and diversity of the data sets produced by today's sequencing and array-based profiling methods present major challenges to visualization tools. The Integrative Genomics Viewer (IGV) is a high-performance viewer that efficiently handles large heterogeneous data sets, while providing a smooth and intuitive user experience at all levels of genome resolution. A key characteristic of IGV is its focus on the integrative nature of genomic studies, with support for both array-based and next-generation sequencing data, and the integration of clinical and phenotypic data. Although IGV is often used to view genomic data from public sources, its primary emphasis is to support researchers who wish to visualize and explore their own data sets or those from colleagues. To that end, IGV supports flexible loading of local and remote data sets, and is optimized to provide high-performance data visualization and exploration on standard desktop systems. \u00a9 The Author(s) 2012. Published by Oxford University Press.","authors":[{"name":"Mesirov J.P."},{"name":"Robinson J.T."},{"name":"Thorvaldsdottir H."}],"citationCount":3988,"date":"2013-03-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"Briefings in Bioinformatics","title":"Integrative Genomics Viewer (IGV): High-performance genomics data visualization and exploration"},"pmcid":"PMC3603213","pmid":"22517427","type":["Primary"]}],"topic":[{"term":"Sequence analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0080"}],"validated":1},"bioschemas":{"name":"IGVtools","home":"https://bio.tools/igvtools","license":"MIT","summary":"The igvtools utility provides a set of tools for pre-processing data files.","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:igvtools/cmd/software.broadinstitute.org","@license":"https://creative